messages:
jess: Quick heads up — PR #4324 landed a streaming example for TS/Py but the pagination example got mutated and CI flagged the Go snippet.

mike: ah, saw the failing test. looks like the Go example uses an older streaming adapter pattern (channels + goroutines) and we changed the cursor shape: now cursor is {position:string} not int.

anna: can we make the examples consistent across langs? my take: show minimal streaming generator + explicit cursor object so it's clear.

sam: agree. propose:

python:
```
def stream_responses(prompt):
    cursor = {"position": ""}
    for chunk in model.stream(prompt, cursor=cursor):
        yield chunk
```

typescript:
```ts
async function* streamResponses(prompt: string) {
  let cursor = { position: "" };
  for await (const chunk of client.stream({ prompt, cursor })) {
    yield chunk;
  }
}
```

go:
```
// simplified: use iterator with cursor struct
type Cursor struct{ Position string }
func StreamResponses(ctx context.Context, prompt string, cursor *Cursor) (<-chan string, error) {
    ch := make(chan string)
    go func(){
        defer close(ch)
        // call runtime streaming API with cursor
    }()
    return ch, nil
}
```

jess: Nice. Two asks: 1) can someone patch the PR with these snippets and note the cursor shape in the migration guide? 2) link to the runtimes spec in the example comment. I can do (2) if folks prefer.

docs-bot: CI: examples-checker failed on 3 files: docs/streaming.md, examples/go/stream.go, examples/ts/stream.ts — see https://ci.internal/reports/4324

mike: I'll open a tiny follow-up PR to fix the Go channel pattern and update tests. leaving the TS/Py snippet edits to docs squad.

anna: I'll update docs/streaming.md to call out cursor object + add short explainer about cancellations and backpressure. will add a short test case for the cursor shape.

sam: tagging @jess for migration note. I can push the TS sample update in the same PR as the docs change if you want.

jess: please do. also add a small note under "breaking changes" (migration guide) — change from numeric offset -> named position key. keep it one sentence.

mike: PR opened: #4331 — fixes go example and unit test. link: https://git.redwood/ri/pr/4331

anna: drafting docs PR now, will reference both 4324 and 4331. will cc @sam for TS patch.

jess: thanks all. small follow-up: after merge, run examples-checker locally (`make examples-check`) to avoid CI churn. :thumbsup:

sam: ack, will run before pushing.

jess: closing thread once PRs merge. ping here when done.
